77 1079 #uuid "35e8275a-bb12-5f98-ba18-184bdee245ee" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423057 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423058 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423063 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423064 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423067 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1077 "selection" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423067 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423078 1079 #uuid "857db1a9-5baa-547f-ad7c-ffed08bafef2" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423065 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423069 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423071 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423073 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423074 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1077 "selection" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423065 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423079 1079 #uuid "aad6b045-a52a-569f-a198-e336ad216b28" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423059 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423061 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423062 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423075 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423076 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1077 "selection" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423076 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423080 1079 #uuid "ac73eb15-075e-5981-aef0-815786fcaa0d" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423081 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423080 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423081 1069 "q-126021" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423081 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423081 1071 "Compute $P(X\\le -4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\le -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x>-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423081 1072 #uuid "3576b4c9-6bad-5c07-bd64-6e08d7444e14" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423081 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -4) & =P(-\\infty <X\\le -4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}]}_{-\\infty }^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423082 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423079 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423082 1069 "q-126017" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423082 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423082 1071 "Compute $P(X>6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423082 1072 #uuid "5cfff2a4-1c49-516b-a57f-2fc4f75675f3" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423082 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =P(6<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{6}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423083 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423078 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423083 1069 "q-160458" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423083 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423083 1071 "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3x-1},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423083 1072 #uuid "5d743af0-a7a6-59cf-8a8b-38734a18e7f0" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423083 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)=3{e}^{3x-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{e}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x-1}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}-0 \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423084 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423077 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423084 1069 "q-160446" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423084 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423084 1071 "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423084 1072 #uuid "7af6cdaa-d1ff-562c-9d47-7e9a37adf5ba" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true] [17592186423084 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534494 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0019d257-76eb-58eb-993a-0411c1c8ea5a" 17592186423057 "answer-0345689f-fc2f-5460-9f38-e059246fb16f" 17592186423058 "answer-06a255f8-64ef-51d8-a6e6-a071190bf006" 17592186423059 "answer-20a4da9c-5ad8-5dda-8ba1-be02f0af04f6" 17592186423060 "answer-23d2d105-cdbc-500b-881f-d9e0d158fa84" 17592186423061 "answer-28421387-3618-5282-a14b-84e4566ab27b" 17592186423062 "answer-4c86aada-f7d7-57c4-bae2-63a127ef9b11" 17592186423063 "answer-56eca2a0-0c43-50ef-b63f-0ce7a632